Coverage does not measure a child process, so a test that runs some measured code itself and starts a child has no row for what the child ran. The selection index now reads the recorder's list of started programs: a test recorded starting a program that can run Python, or with no read record, is never dropped by the file-level narrowing and never narrowed by the by-statement selector (which still only records). Exemptions are by program name: gitleaks and a few programs that only print or wait; git is not exempt in any repository. A git run outside the repository is now recorded (git-elsewhere), so the record version is 3. Also: a test in an xdist group is stored under one spelling. Measured on a full run of this branch: 412 tests held besides the unmeasured ones; 21 test files (70 of 3,229 test-seconds) newly never dropped. Addresses WI-sopig-jarit-hahap-tomab-kanam-katad-huzun-sobus.
